#
# P1-4: innodb_change_buffering=inserts writes the legacy ibuf record
# format (no_counter=true) which cannot carry the functional-field
# flags. At merge time the rebuilt dummy index treats the stored GPP
# column as an ordered field, so re-inserting an ordered key whose
# delete-marked record carries a stale GPP inserts a second physical
# record instead of reviving the old one.
#
# Expected (fixed) behaviour: the merge revives the delete-marked
# record, so a subsequent index scan reads no delete-marked rows.
#
SELECT COUNT(*) AS visible_rows FROM t1 FORCE INDEX (idx_k) WHERE k = 1;
visible_rows
1
include/assert.inc [the re-insert must have gone through the change buffer]
include/assert.inc [ibuf insert merge must revive the delete-marked secondary record]
